435428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435465 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435465 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435465 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435457 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435465 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435465 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435465 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186435432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435465 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ca4abcbb-4080-56b3-9f3e-dfec3322b962" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435467 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435419 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435467 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435467 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435467 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435467 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435455 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435467 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435467 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435467 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186435431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435467 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e4932278-fd35-5668-a02a-427a9d1bc8b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435469 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435469 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163577" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435469 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435469 #edb/ref 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 4\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435469 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "07899bf0-acd5-5cb5-8654-0b2936590b7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435469 #edb/ref 1074 "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=1\\cdot 3=3.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{2}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}[x{y}^{2}]_{x=2}^{x=3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}3{y}^{2}-2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}(\\frac{64}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}\\cdot 21 \\\\  & =7M.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{x}^{2}=7\\,⇒\\,{R}_{x}=\\sqrt{7}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435471 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435471 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163608" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435471 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435471 #edb/ref 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 5\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435471 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "464dc60e-dfa3-5c24-8df3-bdca1e567180" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435471 #edb/ref 1074 "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=3\\cdot 5=15.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{15}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{15}{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{15}{\\int }_{0}^{5}[x{y}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{15}{\\int }_{0}^{5}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{15}[{y}^{3}]_{0}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{15}(125-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{25M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{x}^{2}=\\frac{25}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{3}}=\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435473 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435460 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435473 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163581" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435473 #edb/ref